  "id": "scaling",
  "term": "scaling",
  "definition": "Scaling is the process of determining whether an intervention can be expanded or adapted so it works in broader real-world settings and reaches more people in need. In this context, it also includes using assessments either to refine a program so it fits its delivery setting better or to judge whether wider expansion is feasible.",
